          <Layout class="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.support.JScrollPaneSupportLayout"/>
          <SubComponents>
            <Component class="javax.swing.JTextArea" name="factsTA">
              <Properties>
                <Property name="background" type="java.awt.Color" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.ColorEditor">
                  <Color blue="cc" green="cc" red="cc" type="rgb"/>
                </Property>
                <Property name="columns" type="int" value="20"/>
                <Property name="font" type="java.awt.Font" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.FontEditor">
                  <Font name="Segoe UI" size="10" style="1"/>
                </Property>
                <Property name="rows" type="int" value="5"/>
                <Property name="text" type="java.lang.String" value="(Cool Facts About Dolphins)&#xa;&#xa;1)Dolphins are incredibly smart &#x2014; they can recognize &#xa;themselves in mirrors, use tools, and even &#xa;teach each other skills.&#xa;&#xa;2)They communicate using complex clicks, whistles,&#xa; and body movements.&#xa;&#xa;3)Dolphins can switch off one half of their brain at a&#xa; time while sleeping so they can stay alert for predators&#xa; and breathing.&#xa;&#xa;4)The orca, or killer whale, is actually the largest species&#xa; of dolphin.&#xa;&#xa;5)Dolphins can swim at speeds of 20&#x2013;25 mph, making&#xa; them one of the fastest marine mammals.&#xa;&#xa;(How Sea Pollution Affects Dolphins)&#xa;&#xa;Dolphins suffer massively from polluted oceans. &#xa;Chemicals and microplastics build up in the fish they eat,&#xa; causing health issues, weakened immunity, &#xa;and reproductive problems. Noise pollution from boats&#xa; and industry interferes with their echolocation, making &#xa;it harder for them to hunt and communicate.&#xa; Plastic waste also poses risks of injury or entanglement,&#xa; threatening their survival."/>
              </Properties>
            </Component>
          </SubComponents>
        </Container>
      </SubComponents>
    </Container>
